      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Completion turns zeta and several L-function families into forms where reflection under s ↦ 1-s is explicit, while the xi normalization separates the nontrivial-zero problem from poles and trivial factors. Across the cited cases this is a reusable symmetry interface, not a zero-location theorem.",
