    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_53fe768c6c279ce1c7468cc8b145ac45e39ee075502847f3ea46399fcaf80671",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "After height-dependent unfolding, conjectural and numerical GUE comparisons describe local zero-spacing statistics while discarding absolute height and global arithmetic variation. Separately, rigorous positive-density small-gap information can act as a one-way falsifier: Rodgers-Tao contradict the excessive near-mean gap concentration forced by a hypothetical negative de Bruijn-Newman threshold.",
